From 0626476e9cd167dc0f865303b13e845345af2ca7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Han <danielhanchen@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:27:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] MXFP4 dequant on ROCm: multiply in fp32 and round to 16 bits
 with integer ops

On gfx11 ROCm Triton 3.6 lowers the bf16 x bf16 multiply to v_dot2_bf16_bf16(a, b, +0), which
flushes subnormals and turns -0.0 into +0.0, and an fp32 multiply followed by an fp16 cast to
v_fma_mixlo_f16(a, b, +0), which turns -0.0 into +0.0. The fused kernel then failed its bit-exact
self-check and every gpt-oss expert dequant ran the torch path (~20x slower).

On ROCm the kernel now takes the fp32 path for bf16 too and rounds fp32 -> fp16 / bf16 with an
integer round-to-nearest-even, so no backend combine can fuse the cast. NVIDIA keeps the same
kernel code (EXACT_ROUND is a constexpr, off there). UNSLOTH_MXFP4_EXACT_ROUND=0 / 1 forces it.
